==================================
Updates May '06: Input Decks v0.18
==================================

* New materials added:
  --------------------

   material_14: AlAs
   material_15: InSi
   material_16: SiAs
   material_17: SiP
   material_18: PSi
   material_19: P

* Corrected 20bands parameteres:
  ------------------------------

  Corrected mb_pv according to literature (20-bands) [Phys. Rev. B 66, 125207 
  (2002)]:
  Si 
  GaAs 
  InAs 
  NOTE: InAs and GaAs, both mb_pv AND mb_strain corrected!

* New Solvers (ResFind):
  ----------------------

  Block Lanczos, PCTracemin and PQTracemin, with corresponding options in the 
  BLanczos, PCTracemin_solver and PQTracemin_solver -> 
  -> look for "ResFind" variable and for keywords 'PCTracemin, PQTracemin and 
  BLanczos'
  NOTE: some of the parameters have been re-ordered, Erange is now among the
  options corresponding to Block Lanczos and Lanczos. 


* Options for dumping out the nd_rAtom files:
  -------------------------------------------
  AtomPos option changed to new 3 options, where user can choose to get the 
  rAtom file in equilibrium, after or before strain calculations -> 
  -> look for keywords "AtomPos" in the .xml file.


* E_range:
  --------
  Before this was a general option, now it is inside the Lanczos and Block 
  Lanczos options.
  /Bad news/: when you update your input deck, the Erange is NOT the one you
  previously have, so you'd need to CHANGE IT BY HAND ->  
  -> look for Erange variable.


* Include impurities: 
  -------------------
  Possibility to include impurities (up to 3 for now) and choose the exact
  position where you want them -> 
  -> look for keyword "ImpNumber".


* Enable Efield: 
  --------------
  In opt.ExecParam.Phys, look for "EfieldON", below one can add the x, y, z 
  components -> 
  -> look for keyword "EfieldON", "Ex", "Ey", "Ez"  (Implemented by Rajib, 
  rrahman@purdue.edu).


* Dump Efield/donor file:
  -----------------------
  User can choose to dump in a file the donor potential and/or applied potential
  (perhaps this needs to be polished in ham3d_final.c...)->
  -> look for keyword "donor_file" and "electric_file". 


* 3D Visualization:
  -----------------
  Write output files of dx-format for 3D visualization, if boolean 
  Visualization_3D is set up to 'true'
  -> look for keyword "Visualization_3D" (Implemented by Hoon Ryu, 
  ryu2@purdue.edu). 


* Strain:
  ------
  Possibility to dump out the displacemens for atoms of ONLY the strain domain, 
  by setting boolean "StrainElOnly" to true, in file type '.nd_disp_small'. 
  -> look for keyword "StrainElOnly".
  Likewise, the "TensionOutput" boolean to true will cause the strain tensor to 
  be printed out in a file of type '.nd_exx', '.nd_exy', etc. 
  -> look for keyword "TensionOutput".


* Tilted QWs: 
  -----------
  (Not implemented yet): hkl gives the direction of the tilt with respect to the
  main crystallographic indexes: thus, (1 1 0) is a rotation of 45^\DEG in the 
  XY plane ->
  -> look for keyword "hkl"  

*******************************************************************************
  NOTE: If you have an old input deck (Version = 0.17), you'll need to
  update it to Version 0.18, using the script "update-nemo3d-input.pl",
  which can be found in ~/My_path_to_NEMO_3D/NEMO_3D/nemo3d/misc/:

  > (PATH_TO_UPDATES)/update-nemo3d-input.pl my_input_deck.xml

  where eg. (PATH_TO_UPDATES) = ~/My_path_to_NEMO_3D/NEMO_3D/nemo3d/misc/
  Then, you'll get as an output, your file 'my_input_deck.xm" OVERWRITTEN:
  take this into account, if you want to re-use it!
